Supreme Court, in Municipal Corporation of Delhi Vs. Ghisa Ram (AIR 1967 SC 970),
while examining scope of sub-sec.(2) and (5) of Section 13 of the Act, concluded in clear and unequivocal term that right of accused to get sample examined by the Director of Central Food Laboratory is a valuable right and if this right is infringed,
his conviction cannot be sustained.
